1
00:00:07,934 --> 00:00:13,265
The Life of Muhammadﷺ, The Madinan Period, Volume 1

2
00:00:13,404 --> 00:00:15,410
By Imam Anwar Al_Awlaki,

3
00:00:21,069 --> 00:00:23,158
السلام عليكم ورحمة اللهِ و بركاته

4
00:00:24,370 --> 00:00:27,138
اَعُوْذُ بِاللهِ مِنَّ الشِّيْطَانِ الرَّجِيْمِ ۝ بِسْمِ اللهِ الرَّحْمَانِ الرَّحِيْمَ ۝

5
00:00:27,978 --> 00:00:33,643
اَلْحَمْدُ لله ، وَالصَّلَاةُ وَالسَّلَامُ عَلى سَيِّدِنَا محمد وَعَلَى اَلِهِ وَصَحْبِهِ وَسَلِّمْ تَسْلِيْمًا كَثِيْراَ

6
00:00:34,904 --> 00:00:36,660
One thing that I forgot to mention

7
00:00:37,762 --> 00:00:43,033
when I was talking about the story of the capture of Ummayyah Bin Khalaf(اُمَيَّة بن خَلَف)

8
00:00:44,114 --> 00:00:45,694
by Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف),

9
00:00:46,144 --> 00:00:48,710
When he was held captive by Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف)

10
00:00:49,400 --> 00:00:54,240
and they were walking through the site of the Battle of Badr(بدر).

11
00:00:55,443 --> 00:00:58,526
Ummayyah(أمَيَّة) asked Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن), he said;

12
00:00:58,724 --> 00:01:03,171
who was that man, who had an ostrich feather across his chest?

13
00:01:04,391 --> 00:01:09,798
So, Abdur Rahman Ibn Auf(عبدالرحمن إبن عوف) said, that is Hamza Bin Abdul Muttalib رضي الله عنه,

14
00:01:09,831 --> 00:01:11,199
Ummayyah Bin Khalaf(اُمَيَّة بن خَلَف) said;

15
00:01:11,649 --> 00:01:14,090
هَذَالَّذِيْ فَعَلَ بنا الْأفَاعيْلْ

16
00:01:14,360 --> 00:01:16,365
This is the man who ruined us.

17
00:01:17,607 --> 00:01:21,686
So, Hamza Bin Abdul Muttalib(حمزه بن عبدالمطلب) was truly the lion of Allah,

18
00:01:21,751 --> 00:01:23,535
اَسَدْ الله ورسوله

19
00:01:23,606 --> 00:01:25,209
The lion of Allah and His messenger,

20
00:01:25,510 --> 00:01:28,613
that's something that I just forgot to mention, when I was talking about Ummayyah(أمَيَّه).

21
00:01:28,667 --> 00:01:32,834
 We're gonna carry on, with the prisoners of war, we're still talking about that.

22
00:01:33,843 --> 00:01:36,543
Rasool Allah ﷺ says in a Hadith(حديث) narrated by Abu Dawood(ابوداؤد),

23
00:01:36,961 --> 00:01:43,506
لَوْ كَانَ المُطْعَمْ بِنْ عُدَيْ حَيًّا ثُمَّ كَلَّمَنِيَّ فِيْ هَؤُلَآءِ النَّتَنْى لَتَرَكْتُهُمْ لًهْ

24
00:01:44,450 --> 00:01:48,890
Rasool Allah ﷺ says if Mut'am Ibn Udaye(مطعم إبن عدي) was still alive,

25
00:01:49,417 --> 00:01:52,607
and he talked to me about these prisoners of war,

26
00:01:52,632 --> 00:01:54,415
actually Rasool Allah ﷺ used the word Natan(نتن).

27
00:01:54,804 --> 00:01:57,514
Natan(نتن) means something that has a foul smell.

28
00:01:58,060 --> 00:02:01,394
That is the name that he used to refer to these prisoners of war.

29
00:02:01,842 --> 00:02:07,453
Now probably doesn't literally mean that they were foul smelling,

30
00:02:07,525 --> 00:02:14,180
but what is meant by it is that disbelief is foul smelling, figuratively speaking,

31
00:02:14,260 --> 00:02:17,313
 because Allah has called it Rijs(رجس), impurity

32
00:02:17,920 --> 00:02:20,421
so disbelief is an impure thing.

33
00:02:20,731 --> 00:02:23,600
Anyway, Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying the meaning of the Hadith(حديث).

34
00:02:24,583 --> 00:02:30,959
If Mut'am Ibn Udaye(مطعم إبن عدي), If he was alive, and he interceded for these prisoners of war,

35
00:02:30,984 --> 00:02:32,874
I would have released them, for him.

36
00:02:33,825 --> 00:02:42,928
Rasool Allah ﷺ is telling us that he was grateful to Al-Mut'am Ibn Udaye(المطعم إبن عدي).

37
00:02:43,531 --> 00:02:44,635
 Who was a disbeliever

38
00:02:45,321 --> 00:02:51,729
because of his honesty and his good stand towards the Muslims,

39
00:02:51,896 --> 00:02:54,407
even though he was a Mushrik(مشرك) a disbelievers.

40
00:02:55,899 --> 00:03:03,950
And this shows that Rasool Allah ﷺ would act appropriately,

41
00:03:04,962 --> 00:03:09,212
according to the deeds of a person.

42
00:03:10,190 --> 00:03:13,655
So, he would deal with good people Kindly

43
00:03:13,823 --> 00:03:17,714
and he would deal with evil people accordingly.

44
00:03:18,813 --> 00:03:22,266
Now, we don't want to go into either extreme

45
00:03:22,702 --> 00:03:30,010
of being incapable of showing nothing but brutality towards the Kuffar(كفار)

46
00:03:30,717 --> 00:03:38,668
or on the other hand to act in a way that only shows that we are interested in appeasing the Kuffar(كفار).

47
00:03:40,147 --> 00:03:46,406
A Muslim should act in each situation and make a judgment in that situation

48
00:03:46,758 --> 00:03:51,953
according to what is the most wise method of action.

49
00:03:52,620 --> 00:03:55,365
And one should overcome emotions

50
00:03:55,658 --> 00:04:00,951
and one should overcome doing something because of, I'm worried what other people will say,

51
00:04:01,185 --> 00:04:04,403
I'm worried, how our perception will be seen.

52
00:04:04,755 --> 00:04:07,997
I'm worried that I will be giving Islam, a bad picture,

53
00:04:08,134 --> 00:04:10,085
I'm worried about this, I'm worried about that.

54
00:04:10,189 --> 00:04:13,909
We should forget about all of these considerations and do what is right

55
00:04:14,491 --> 00:04:16,249
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying here

56
00:04:16,538 --> 00:04:19,969
if this man was alive, I would have released these prisoners of war for him.

57
00:04:22,595 --> 00:04:23,652
On the other hand,

58
00:04:24,135 --> 00:04:34,114
Rasool Allah ﷺ, specifically chose Uqba Bin Abi Moait(عقبة بن أبي معيط) and An-Nadhar Bin Haris(نضر بن حارث) to be executed

59
00:04:34,345 --> 00:04:39,231
 from among all of the other prisoners of war, which totaled 70.

60
00:04:39,255 --> 00:04:41,286
The number of prisoners of war was 70.

61
00:04:41,735 --> 00:04:45,925
Rasool Allah ﷺ calls Uqba Bin Abi Moait(عقبة بن أبي معيط),

62
00:04:46,438 --> 00:04:47,995
and Uqba Bin Abi Moait(عقبة بن أبي معيط) said;

63
00:04:48,046 --> 00:04:54,811
How come, O Messenger of Allah you are choosing me out of everyone else to be killed.

64
00:04:55,359 --> 00:05:01,904
 O messenger of Allah, if you're gonna kill the rest of the prisoners of war then kill me with them,

65
00:05:02,277 --> 00:05:05,769
if you're gonna ransom them, than ransom me with them.

66
00:05:06,086 --> 00:05:10,504
How come you are picking me out of everyone else to be executed?

67
00:05:11,448 --> 00:05:12,546
Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

68
00:05:12,586 --> 00:05:14,696
لِعَدَوَتِكَ لِلهِ وَرَسُوْلِه

69
00:05:15,002 --> 00:05:17,875
Because of your animosity towards Allah and His messenger.

70
00:05:18,125 --> 00:05:19,303
So, Uqba(عُقْبَة) said;

71
00:05:19,635 --> 00:05:21,006
فَمَنْ لِّسِّبِيَّهْ

72
00:05:21,410 --> 00:05:22,745
Who will take care of my children.?

73
00:05:22,785 --> 00:05:25,176
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him, the fire.

74
00:05:25,517 --> 00:05:27,565
قَدِّمْه’ يَا عَاصِمْ اَضْرِبْ عُنُقَهْ

75
00:05:27,645 --> 00:05:31,397
O Asim(عاصم) Pull him forward and behead him.

76
00:05:32,671 --> 00:05:38,419
And he was promptly beheaded by Asim Bin Thabit رضي الله عنه.

77
00:05:39,323 --> 00:05:41,214
While An-Nadhar Bin Haris(النضر بن حارث) also,

78
00:05:41,239 --> 00:05:44,831
Rasool Allah ﷺ, told Ali Ibn Abi Talib(علي ابن ابي طالب) to execute him.

79
00:05:45,062 --> 00:05:48,507
These two men were specifically handpicked, out of everyone else

80
00:05:48,543 --> 00:05:53,575
because of their evil and Ibn Kathir رضي الله عنه said;

81
00:05:54,019 --> 00:05:58,455
I would comment that these two men were among the most evil of Allah's servants,

82
00:05:58,844 --> 00:06:03,306
the most stubborn, wicked, envious and disbelieving of men

83
00:06:03,716 --> 00:06:08,849
and they had been very active in satirizing Islam and its supporters,

84
00:06:09,232 --> 00:06:12,046
 Allah damn them, and he did, indeed.

85
00:06:13,430 --> 00:06:15,481
Uqba Bin Abi Moait(عقبة بن أبي معيط) was the one

86
00:06:16,104 --> 00:06:19,676
who saw Rasool Allah ﷺ in Sujood(سجود) next to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه),

87
00:06:20,100 --> 00:06:21,860
when Rasool Allah ﷺ was still in Makkah

88
00:06:22,467 --> 00:06:24,531
and he stepped over his neck with his foot.

89
00:06:25,287 --> 00:06:29,106
Rasool Allah ﷺ said, I felt that my eyes were going to pop out

90
00:06:30,030 --> 00:06:31,314
I was gonna die.

91
00:06:32,050 --> 00:06:35,314
And this is also the man who saw me in Rukkoo(ركوع)

92
00:06:35,784 --> 00:06:42,986
and came in threw the intestines of a camel, he threw them over my back

93
00:06:43,433 --> 00:06:47,011
and then Fatimah رضي الله عنها came and remove them.

94
00:06:48,214 --> 00:06:52,268
So, Uqba Bin Abi Moait(عقبة بن أبي معيط) was one of the worst devils of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

95
00:06:53,153 --> 00:06:56,107
And that is why he deserved this severe punishment.

96
00:06:56,662 --> 00:07:00,410
While An-Nadhar Bin Haris(النضر بن حارث) was the one who went to Persia,

97
00:07:00,727 --> 00:07:03,946
to learn the stories of Asfandyaar(أسفند يار) and Rustum(رستم),

98
00:07:04,422 --> 00:07:08,842
and he would come back to Makkah, and tell the people to gather around him and he would say,

99
00:07:08,975 --> 00:07:12,147
come and listen to my stories, they're better than Muhammad(محمد)'s stories.

100
00:07:12,309 --> 00:07:17,053
what makes him more befitting to being a prophet compared to me?

101
00:07:17,402 --> 00:07:20,111
He said, I can tell stories just like he could.

102
00:07:20,602 --> 00:07:28,327
So, what makes him entitled to becoming a prophet, and doesn't give me that right.?

103
00:07:29,345 --> 00:07:35,398
So, he used to sway the people away from the Majlis(مجلس) circle of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

104
00:07:35,722 --> 00:07:37,452
So, these two men were executed.

105
00:07:37,846 --> 00:07:42,714
So you can contrast this to what Rasool Allah ﷺ said about Al-Mutam Ibn Udae(ألمطعم إبن عدي)

106
00:07:42,885 --> 00:07:46,524
and see how Rasool Allah ﷺ would deal differently with different people.

107
00:07:46,575 --> 00:07:50,338
Now, with these two men, they were executed.

108
00:07:51,175 --> 00:07:59,637
However, with the rest, Rasool Allah ﷺ specifically gave the instructions to the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم and said;

109
00:07:59,952 --> 00:08:02,483
اِسْتَوْصُوْا اَسَرَى خَيْرًا

110
00:08:02,837 --> 00:08:05,665
Treat the prisoners of war kindly,

111
00:08:06,356 --> 00:08:07,396
treat them kindly.

112
00:08:07,962 --> 00:08:12,286
So, Abu Aziz(ابو عزيز), the brother of Mus'ab Bin Umair(مصعب إبن عمير) he said;

113
00:08:12,598 --> 00:08:17,935
كُنْتُ فِيْ الْأَسَارَى يَوْمَ بَدْرٍ، فَقَالَ رَسُول الله صلى الله عليه وسلم اِسْتَوْصُوْ بِلْاَسَرَى خَيْرًا

114
00:08:18,318 --> 00:08:22,253
وَكُنْتُ فِيْ نَفَرٍ مِنَّ الْأَنْصَارِ فَكَانُوْا إِذَا قَدّمُوْا عَشَاءَهُمْ

115
00:08:22,528 --> 00:08:27,238
اَوْغَدَاءَهُمْ أَكَّلُوْا التَّمْرَ وَاَطْعَمُوْنِيْ الْبُرَّة (خَصّونِي بالخبز) ؛ لِوَصِيَّةِ رَسول الله

116
00:08:28,221 --> 00:08:32,629
He said, I was with a group of Ansaar(اَنْصَار), bringing me from Badr(بدر),

117
00:08:33,398 --> 00:08:35,922
when they had their lunch and dinner,

118
00:08:35,962 --> 00:08:39,809
 they would give me the bread and ate the dates themselves,

119
00:08:39,982 --> 00:08:45,693
in accordance with instruction given them by Rasool Allah ﷺ regarding us,

120
00:08:46,204 --> 00:08:51,622
every piece of bread that came into their hands, they passed on to me,

121
00:08:52,189 --> 00:08:57,694
I was embarrassed and would return the bread, but they would pass it back untouched.

122
00:08:58,296 --> 00:09:01,116
Bread was the better food compared to dates,

123
00:09:01,505 --> 00:09:04,223
so they would eat the dates and they would give him the bread.

124
00:09:05,524 --> 00:09:08,002
And they would just survive on eating dates.

125
00:09:08,411 --> 00:09:14,691
So, they would give him actually they would give him a better treatment, than they would give themselves.

126
00:09:16,315 --> 00:09:18,563
Ibn Hishaam(إبن هشام), he comments on this. He said;

127
00:09:18,923 --> 00:09:24,823
This Abu Aziz(ابوعزيز) was the standard bearer of the Mushrikeen(مشركين) at Badr(بدر), following An-Nadhar Bin Haris(النضر بن حارث).

128
00:09:25,328 --> 00:09:27,778
So, Abu Aziz(ابوعزيز) wasn't just a foot soldier

129
00:09:27,970 --> 00:09:31,397
Abu Aziz(ابو عزيز) was the standard bearer on the Battle of Badr(بدر)

130
00:09:31,727 --> 00:09:37,850
and still Rasool Allah ﷺ has told to treat such men, well.

131
00:09:39,548 --> 00:09:41,700
Abul Aas Bin Ar-Rabiy(ابوالعاص بن الربيع), he said;

132
00:09:42,117 --> 00:09:45,147
كُنْتُ فِيْ رَاهط مِّنَّ الْاَنْصَارِ جَزَآءَهُمُ اللهُ خَيْرًا

133
00:09:45,457 --> 00:09:48,437
كُنَّا اِذَ تَعَشَّيْنَا اَوْ تَغَدَّيْنَا آثرُوْنِيْ بِالخُبْزْ

134
00:09:48,566 --> 00:09:49,981
Pretty much the same thing.

135
00:09:50,363 --> 00:09:52,566
Al-Waleed Bin Waleed Bin Mugheera(ألوليد بن وليد بن مغيرة), he would say;

136
00:09:52,606 --> 00:09:54,579
 وَكَانُوْ يَحْمِلُوْنَنَا وَيَمْشُوْنْ

137
00:09:54,830 --> 00:09:56,971
They would walk while we would ride.

138
00:09:57,440 --> 00:09:59,377
So, the prisoners of war are riding,

139
00:09:59,828 --> 00:10:02,010
while the Sahabah رضي الله عنهم are walking.

140
00:10:03,560 --> 00:10:05,280
And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله),

141
00:10:05,735 --> 00:10:12,491
see this good treatment is what caused many of these prisoners of war to become Muslim.

142
00:10:12,990 --> 00:10:17,203
Throughout the battles of Rasool Allah ﷺ, we would hear about people who were arrested or captured

143
00:10:17,241 --> 00:10:19,359
 and then they would become Muslim and stayed behind.

144
00:10:21,142 --> 00:10:28,569
And some of them to show and prove that they're not becoming Muslim for fear of the sword.

145
00:10:29,059 --> 00:10:32,256
After they are released, they would go back to their people

146
00:10:32,284 --> 00:10:35,396
and then they would come back to Rasool Allah ﷺ and become Muslim.

147
00:10:35,852 --> 00:10:39,249
To prove that we have became Muslim of our own initiative,

148
00:10:39,274 --> 00:10:42,467
not because any pressure, we weren't pressured into it.

149
00:10:43,827 --> 00:10:45,942
For example, Abu Aziz(ابو عزيز), he ended up becoming Muslim.

150
00:10:45,982 --> 00:10:48,971
The brother of Mus'ab Ibn Umair(مصعب ابن عمير), when he saw, how the Muslims were treating him.

151
00:10:49,479 --> 00:10:51,413
They would treat him better than their own selves

152
00:10:52,000 --> 00:10:54,863
So, Akhlaaq(أخلاق) are important even with your enemy,

153
00:10:55,133 --> 00:11:00,400
even with the enemy, the Muslim should deal with him, in a good way with dignity.

154
00:11:01,484 --> 00:11:06,643
I mean, a Muslim is not cruel, a Muslim is not wicked, a Muslim is not deceptive,

155
00:11:07,057 --> 00:11:08,655
a Muslim is not a liar,

156
00:11:09,103 --> 00:11:14,776
a Muslim deals with everyone with honesty, dignity, straightforwardness

157
00:11:15,162 --> 00:11:17,689
and kindness towards all of the creation of Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

158
00:11:17,729 --> 00:11:24,950
except those who deserve to be dealt cruelly like Uqba Bin Abi Moait(عقبة بن أبي معيط), and An-Nadhar Bin Haris(النضر بن حارث)

159
00:11:25,101 --> 00:11:30,303
because these are people who are so evil you can't afford, treating them kindly,

160
00:11:31,126 --> 00:11:34,979
treating them kindly is actually being fooled by them,

161
00:11:35,685 --> 00:11:40,248
because these are people who are going to turn around and harm the Muslims.

162
00:11:42,066 --> 00:11:47,167
Al-Abbas Ibn Abdul Muttalib(العباس بن عبدالمطلب), the uncle of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

163
00:11:48,120 --> 00:11:50,636
Rasool Ullah صلوات الله وسلام عليه said;

164
00:11:50,780 --> 00:11:53,976
Ransom yourself, pay your ransom.

165
00:11:54,784 --> 00:11:59,464
 Al-Abbas(العباس) said, O Messenger of Allah, I'm a Muslim.

166
00:12:00,962 --> 00:12:02,645
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him;

167
00:12:03,371 --> 00:12:06,454
اَمَّا ظَاهِرُكَ فَكَانَ عَلَيْنَا

168
00:12:07,538 --> 00:12:10,750
What was evident was that you were against us.

169
00:12:10,886 --> 00:12:13,654
Allah knows best about your accepting Islam.

170
00:12:14,392 --> 00:12:17,131
Rasool Allah ﷺ is here setting for us, a rule,

171
00:12:17,698 --> 00:12:19,590
We go by what we see.

172
00:12:20,396 --> 00:12:25,041
We do not and cannot know what is in the hearts.

173
00:12:26,759 --> 00:12:29,389
Only Allahعَزّوجَلّ is, the One, Who can see the hearts,

174
00:12:30,645 --> 00:12:31,951
we go by what we see. R

175
00:12:32,067 --> 00:12:34,101
asool Allah ﷺ is telling Al-Abbas(العباس),

176
00:12:34,534 --> 00:12:36,789
Allah is the one who knows whether you're Muslim or not,

177
00:12:36,834 --> 00:12:38,811
what we can see is that you were against us,

178
00:12:38,937 --> 00:12:41,510
you were fighting us, you were in the army of the enemy.

179
00:12:42,210 --> 00:12:43,585
So, we're going to go by that

180
00:12:43,696 --> 00:12:46,015
and Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمرابن الخطاب), he said, when he was Khalifah(خليفه),

181
00:12:46,714 --> 00:12:48,317
In the time of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

182
00:12:48,565 --> 00:12:51,638
Revelation would come down and tell us, what is in the hearts of men.

183
00:12:52,192 --> 00:12:55,570
But now we're going to go by what we see.

184
00:12:55,979 --> 00:12:59,567
We're going to make our judgments based on what appears from you.

185
00:13:00,035 --> 00:13:04,060
If what appears from you is Islam, we will accept that,

186
00:13:04,440 --> 00:13:06,896
and if what appears from you is disbelief,

187
00:13:07,344 --> 00:13:10,015
we will assume that you are disbeliever,

188
00:13:10,648 --> 00:13:13,274
even if you claim that you are otherwise.

189
00:13:13,751 --> 00:13:16,880
If your actions are those of a disbeliever

190
00:13:17,408 --> 00:13:20,336
it doesn't benefit you to say that you are a Muslim,

191
00:13:20,890 --> 00:13:22,779
We will go by your actions.

192
00:13:23,480 --> 00:13:26,363
So, the action of Al-Abbas(العباس) here was, that he was with the enemy

193
00:13:27,208 --> 00:13:30,344
You can claim that you are a Muslim, you can state;

194
00:13:30,503 --> 00:13:31,639
لا اله الا الله

195
00:13:31,688 --> 00:13:35,180
But why were you on the enemies side.?

196
00:13:36,046 --> 00:13:37,468
And this is a very important rule,

197
00:13:37,897 --> 00:13:43,031
we should not judge people, according to what is in their hearts, we judge them by their action.

198
00:13:43,400 --> 00:13:47,454
In the same time, we don't allow people to fool us by stating,

199
00:13:47,881 --> 00:13:51,393
that they are this and that when their actions prove otherwise.

200
00:13:51,761 --> 00:13:56,992
we go by the actions of people that is how we judge people.

201
00:13:58,176 --> 00:14:01,794
So, somebody who's acting as a disbeliever in and out,

202
00:14:02,333 --> 00:14:05,589
cannot come on fool us and trick us and say; I'm a Muslim

203
00:14:07,168 --> 00:14:08,747
Al-Abbas(العباس) said; I don't have any money.

204
00:14:09,266 --> 00:14:13,951
Rasool Allahﷺ told him; What about the money that you buried in the ground,

205
00:14:14,384 --> 00:14:19,891
and you told your wife, Ummal-Fadhal(أم الفضل), if I am killed, then make use of this money.

206
00:14:20,398 --> 00:14:24,396
Al-Abbas(العباس) said: I testify and bear witness that you are a messenger of Allah,

207
00:14:24,436 --> 00:14:28,112
 no one knew of that treasure of mine, except me and my wife.

208
00:14:29,791 --> 00:14:32,714
So, he did pay for his ransom.

209
00:14:33,098 --> 00:14:35,511
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ revealed the Ayah(آية);

210
00:14:36,114 --> 00:14:45,150
يَا أَيُّهَا النَّبِيُّ قُلْ لِمَنْ فِي أَيْدِيكُمْ مِنَ الْأَسْرَىٰ

211
00:14:45,348 --> 00:14:57,411
إِنْ يَعْلَمِ اللَّهُ فِي قُلُوبِكُمْ خَيْرًا يُؤْتِكُمْ خَيْرًا مِمَّا أُخِذَ مِنْكُمْ وَيَغْفِرْ لَكُمْ ۗ

212
00:14:57,705 --> 00:15:01,230
وَاللَّهُ غَفُورٌ رَحِيمٌ ّ۝

213
00:15:01,500 --> 00:15:13,215
وَإِنْ يُرِيدُوا خِيَانَتَكَ فَقَدْ خَانُوا اللَّهَ مِنْ قَبْلُ فَأَمْكَنَ مِنْهُمْ ۗ وَاللَّهُ عَلِيمٌ حَكِيمٌ۝

214
00:15:13,971 --> 00:15:18,492
O Prophet, say to whoever is in your hands of the captives.

215
00:15:20,210 --> 00:15:24,873
If Allah knows any good in your hearts,

216
00:15:25,461 --> 00:15:29,045
He will give you better than what was taken from you,

217
00:15:29,836 --> 00:15:33,424
and He will forgive you and Allah's Forgiving and Merciful.

218
00:15:34,745 --> 00:15:36,964
But if they intend to betray you,

219
00:15:37,241 --> 00:15:39,972
 Then they have already betrayed Allah before

220
00:15:40,092 --> 00:15:44,212
and he empowered you over them and Allah is Knowing and Wise.

221
00:15:44,898 --> 00:15:48,555
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ is telling these, men who claim that they were Muslim

222
00:15:48,595 --> 00:15:50,142
 and they had to pay for the ransom.

223
00:15:50,435 --> 00:15:51,754
If you are Muslim,

224
00:15:52,008 --> 00:15:55,649
Allahعَزّوجَلّ will replace that money that was taken from you, Don't worry.!

225
00:15:56,248 --> 00:16:00,673
Al-Abbas(العباس) said that I paid 20 Uoqia(أوقيه) of gold.

226
00:16:00,744 --> 00:16:04,348
 This is a certain weight of gold, I paid that for my ransom.

227
00:16:04,658 --> 00:16:08,229
 And then Allahعَزّوجَلّ has given me much more than that.

228
00:16:08,836 --> 00:16:12,880
Meaning Allahعَزّوجَلّ has replaced that money that he paid for ransom

229
00:16:13,387 --> 00:16:19,942
and Allahعَزّوجَلّ has multiplied it for Al-Abbas Bin Abdul Muttalib رضي الله عنه.

230
00:16:21,085 --> 00:16:27,850
Abul Aas(ابو العاص) was the husband of Zainab(زينب) Bint(بنت) Rasool Allah ﷺ.

231
00:16:29,040 --> 00:16:30,106
He was a Mushrik(مشرك),

232
00:16:30,847 --> 00:16:35,415
so the daughter of Rasool Allah ﷺ up until that point was married to a disbelievers.

233
00:16:35,471 --> 00:16:44,135
This was before the ruling came down preventing Muslim women from remaining with their disbelieving husbands,

234
00:16:44,783 --> 00:16:46,191
this was before that ruling.

235
00:16:47,057 --> 00:16:48,477
And she was in Makkah,

236
00:16:49,495 --> 00:16:55,091
so she wants to free her husband,

237
00:16:55,544 --> 00:16:58,764
Zainab(زينب) Bint Rasool Allah ﷺ, she wants to free her husband Al-Aas(ألعاص).

238
00:16:59,661 --> 00:17:04,514
So, let me read to you what Ibn Is'haaq(ابن اسحاق) said about this situation.

239
00:17:06,133 --> 00:17:10,738
Actually, I will read you the story of her coming back.

240
00:17:11,075 --> 00:17:14,648
But before that let's just talk about the ransoming.

241
00:17:15,809 --> 00:17:26,295
So, Zainabرضي الله عنها , she sends an amount of money sufficient to release her husband from captivity.

242
00:17:27,396 --> 00:17:30,799
She also sends along with that money a necklace.

243
00:17:32,919 --> 00:17:38,119
This necklace was given to her as a gift by her mother Khadijah(خديجه),

244
00:17:38,856 --> 00:17:39,739
when she got married.

245
00:17:41,080 --> 00:17:43,056
This was her wedding gift, from her mother.

246
00:17:44,091 --> 00:17:45,734
So, the necklace belonged to Khadijah(خديجه)

247
00:17:45,966 --> 00:17:49,399
and then Khadijah(خديجه) gave it as a gift to her daughter when she got married.

248
00:17:50,404 --> 00:17:52,702
So, Zainab(زينب) sends this necklace.

249
00:17:54,120 --> 00:17:57,380
When the necklace falls in the hands of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

250
00:17:57,899 --> 00:18:03,906
it brought back memories of his wife Khadijah رحمة الله عليها,

251
00:18:04,669 --> 00:18:13,235
and we know that Rasool Allah ﷺ was very soft hearted, kind, compassionate and this touched him.

252
00:18:13,536 --> 00:18:20,214
 So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told the Ansaar(أنصار) who were holding her husband.

253
00:18:21,119 --> 00:18:26,848
He said: If you should think fit to deliver her prisoner to her,

254
00:18:27,316 --> 00:18:30,086
 and to return to her, what is hers then do so.

255
00:18:31,070 --> 00:18:33,173
And they immediately released him

256
00:18:33,629 --> 00:18:35,431
and they released them without ransom.

257
00:18:35,931 --> 00:18:38,405
 And they sent back also the necklace.

258
00:18:38,873 --> 00:18:46,789
Now Rasool Allah ﷺ, placed a condition on the release of Abul Aas(ابوالعاص).

259
00:18:47,645 --> 00:18:54,977
And that condition was you never assist an enemy against us,

260
00:18:55,477 --> 00:18:59,273
and you send to me, Zainab(زينب).

261
00:19:00,574 --> 00:19:03,379
So, Abul Aas(ابوالعاص) was a man of his word.

262
00:19:04,381 --> 00:19:06,114
When he went back to Makkah

263
00:19:06,588 --> 00:19:12,403
He allowed Zainab(زينب) to leave Makkah and go to her father.

264
00:19:13,154 --> 00:19:17,508
Ibn Is'haaq says; so she continued making plans.

265
00:19:18,195 --> 00:19:25,906
When she was ready, her husband's brother, Kinanah Ibn Rabiyah(كنانة إبن ربيعه) brought a camel which she mounted.

266
00:19:26,448 --> 00:19:29,780
 And he taking his bow and quiver, led her away.

267
00:19:30,923 --> 00:19:34,498
She riding in a Haudaj(هودج), and it being daytime.

268
00:19:35,343 --> 00:19:38,744
Some of the Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) men discussed this and followed after her

269
00:19:39,124 --> 00:19:41,352
catching up with her Dhu Tuwaa(ذو طوى),

270
00:19:42,605 --> 00:19:48,008
the first to reach her was Habbar Ibn Aswad Ibn Al-Muttalib(هبار إبن أسود إبن المطلب).

271
00:19:49,120 --> 00:19:54,319
He scared her with his spear as she was there in the Haudaj(هودج).

272
00:19:54,748 --> 00:19:59,934
And because as they claimed, she was pregnant at the time, she suffered a miscarriage.

273
00:20:01,248 --> 00:20:06,498
Her brother in law then knelt down and took the arrows from his quiver, saying,

274
00:20:06,744 --> 00:20:10,955
 By Allah, if any man comes near me, I'll put an arrow into him,

275
00:20:11,641 --> 00:20:13,616
the man drew away from him.

276
00:20:14,977 --> 00:20:18,743
Then Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) arrived with some other Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) leaders and said,

277
00:20:19,311 --> 00:20:21,937
Put down your arrows, so we can talk with you.

278
00:20:22,696 --> 00:20:27,134
He did so and Abu Sufiyan(ابوسفيان) drew near him and said;

279
00:20:27,399 --> 00:20:29,428
You have not done well.

280
00:20:30,118 --> 00:20:34,309
You came forth with a woman openly going over people's heads,

281
00:20:34,690 --> 00:20:39,130
even though you're aware of the injury and damage done us by Muhammad(محمد).

282
00:20:39,878 --> 00:20:43,680
When you took away his daughter openly, and regardless of anyone else,

283
00:20:44,083 --> 00:20:47,546
that people thought this was due to the humiliation we have undergone,

284
00:20:47,857 --> 00:20:51,179
and that this reflected our weakness and in capacity,

285
00:20:51,520 --> 00:20:54,150
 I swear we don't want to keep her from her father

286
00:20:54,618 --> 00:20:55,994
and we're not after revenge.

287
00:20:56,542 --> 00:21:02,182
But you'd better return back then you can secretly take her away to her father.

288
00:21:03,462 --> 00:21:07,487
So it shows you, that these Kuffar(كفار) of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), they respected woman,

289
00:21:08,886 --> 00:21:16,319
unlike some of the enemies of Allahعَزّوجَلّ, today who are willing to violate the rights of Muslim women and Muslim children,

290
00:21:16,707 --> 00:21:20,626
but these Kuffar(كفار) they still had some dignity in their hearts and Abu Sufiyan(ابو سفيان) said,

291
00:21:20,935 --> 00:21:24,053
as long as you're going to take her away secretly, we don't have a problem with that.

292
00:21:25,342 --> 00:21:27,821
Anyway, and she reached Madina safely.

293
00:21:29,003 --> 00:21:30,850
Abu Izza(أبوعزة) another prisoner of war,

294
00:21:31,537 --> 00:21:35,980
he said, O Messenger of Allah, You know, my state of finances,

295
00:21:36,349 --> 00:21:38,332
I am poor and have a family.

296
00:21:38,658 --> 00:21:40,181
So, be gracious to me.

297
00:21:41,195 --> 00:21:45,529
Abu Izza(أبوعزة) had daughters to take care of, and he was poor.

298
00:21:46,396 --> 00:21:52,584
Rasool Allah ﷺ appreciated, he was consider it of his situation.

299
00:21:53,567 --> 00:21:58,776
So he told him, I'm gonna allow you to be freed.

300
00:21:58,983 --> 00:22:04,512
 However my condition is that you do not support anyone else against me.

301
00:22:05,274 --> 00:22:08,554
This time you came out fighting against me in the Battle of Badr(بدر),

302
00:22:09,756 --> 00:22:13,475
next time you refuse to fight against Muhammadﷺ and the Muslims.

303
00:22:14,459 --> 00:22:15,838
Abu Izza(أبوعزة) agreed.

304
00:22:16,242 --> 00:22:24,250
However, in the Battle of Uhud(أحد), the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), were able to seduce him, into joining them.

305
00:22:24,657 --> 00:22:29,888
 And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله), again, he fell into the hands of the Muslims.

306
00:22:31,149 --> 00:22:34,319
This time he tried to use the same excuse again,

307
00:22:34,805 --> 00:22:39,138
and said; O Messenger of Allah, I have daughters, I'm poor, let me go.

308
00:22:40,078 --> 00:22:45,266
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him, I will not let you stroke your beard and say,

309
00:22:45,450 --> 00:22:47,918
that you have deceived Muhammad(محمد) twice.

310
00:22:48,999 --> 00:22:57,293
So, Muhammadﷺ wasn't sentimental, and he wasn't a leader that could be tricked or deceived.

311
00:22:58,075 --> 00:23:01,305
He was kind, he was compassionate, he was tolerant,

312
00:23:01,739 --> 00:23:08,190
but in the same time, he would not allow people to take advantage of these good qualities and harm the Muslims.

313
00:23:08,744 --> 00:23:13,811
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ told him, I already allowed you once I'm not gonna allow you again.

314
00:23:14,247 --> 00:23:18,013
 And he ordered his execution, at the spot.

315
00:23:19,172 --> 00:23:24,406
And Rasool Allah ﷺ said: A believer will not be bitten twice from the same layer.

316
00:23:24,962 --> 00:23:26,835
A believer will not be tricked twice,

317
00:23:26,915 --> 00:23:32,390
a believer should not allow himself to be bitten twice from the same source.

318
00:23:33,236 --> 00:23:35,475
So, this is an important lesson for the Muslims.

319
00:23:35,936 --> 00:23:43,306
We shouldn't be gullible and fall prey to deceptive words,

320
00:23:43,756 --> 00:23:52,586
muslims should be alert and should know what and who are their benifit islam and muslims

321
00:23:52,665 --> 00:23:54,536
 and who are up to no good.

322
00:23:55,691 --> 00:23:58,028
Suhail Ibn Amr(سهيل إبن عمرو), one of the nobility,

323
00:23:59,002 --> 00:24:01,124
one of the leaders of the people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

324
00:24:02,720 --> 00:24:06,175
He was taken as a POW.

325
00:24:06,702 --> 00:24:08,032
He used to speak against Islam.

326
00:24:08,072 --> 00:24:11,412
He was a fluent and good eloquent speaker.

327
00:24:12,247 --> 00:24:15,753
So, Umar Bin Khattabرضي الله عنه said;

328
00:24:16,991 --> 00:24:22,140
O Rasool Ullah; "Let me extract, the two front teeth of Suhail Ibn Amr(سهيل إبن عمرو),

329
00:24:22,913 --> 00:24:27,219
so his tongue will protrude and he will never speak ill of you again.

330
00:24:28,569 --> 00:24:34,846
Umar Bin Khattab(عمر بن خطاب) wanted to mutilate his mouth pull out his teeth,

331
00:24:35,330 --> 00:24:37,943
 so that he won't be able to speak properly again.

332
00:24:38,649 --> 00:24:43,323
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; I will not mutilate him,

333
00:24:43,853 --> 00:24:46,793
because Allah could mutilate me,

334
00:24:46,872 --> 00:24:55,349
meaning this is not the Islamic way, treating enemies even if they are enemies

335
00:24:56,095 --> 00:24:58,595
 and Rasool Allah ﷺ then said;

336
00:24:58,963 --> 00:25:03,341
"Maybe he will take a stand for which you will not criticize him."

337
00:25:04,227 --> 00:25:09,103
Maybe one day, this tongue of his, which was used for evil,

338
00:25:09,588 --> 00:25:11,475
will be an instrument of good.

339
00:25:11,834 --> 00:25:16,975
And Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله) that did happen as Rasool Allah ﷺ stated,

340
00:25:17,622 --> 00:25:21,647
when Rasool Allah ﷺ died and all of the Arabs apostated.

341
00:25:22,023 --> 00:25:28,826
Suhail Ibn Amr(سهيل إبن عمرو), was the reason, for the steadfastness of the people of Makkah.

342
00:25:29,153 --> 00:25:30,390
He stood up and said;

343
00:25:30,588 --> 00:25:38,432
يَا مَعْشَرَقُرَيْشْ لَا تَكُوْنُوْا آخِرَ النَّاسِ اِسْلَامًا وَاَوَّلَّهُمْ رِدَّةْ مَنْ رَابَنَا ضَرَبْنَا عُنُقَا

344
00:25:38,539 --> 00:25:44,962
O people of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ), Don't be the last people to enter Islam and the first people to leave it.

345
00:25:45,982 --> 00:25:49,417
Whoever we are suspicious of, we will behead him.

346
00:25:50,829 --> 00:25:54,655
And these words kept the people of Makkah firm on Islam,

347
00:25:55,096 --> 00:25:58,352
even though they were new Muslims and their Islam could have been weak,

348
00:25:58,846 --> 00:26:02,282
because it didn't take deep roots in their hearts yet,

349
00:26:02,599 --> 00:26:07,930
but because of these words of Suhail Ibn Amr(سهيل إبن عمرو), they remained Muslims.

350
00:26:09,107 --> 00:26:13,285
Rasool Allah ﷺ told the prisoners of war,

351
00:26:13,467 --> 00:26:17,619
who could teach reading and writing, the ones who were illiterate.

352
00:26:18,722 --> 00:26:25,911
He said, If you teach 10 children to read and write, that will be your ransom, you will be freed.

353
00:26:26,578 --> 00:26:32,670
And this shows you the importance that was placed on literacy and on education,

354
00:26:32,806 --> 00:26:34,749
اِقْرَأْ بِاسْمِ رَبِّكَ الَّذِي خَلَقَ

355
00:26:34,947 --> 00:26:39,076
were the first Ayaat(آيات) revealed to Rasool Allah ﷺ.

356
00:26:40,026 --> 00:26:44,787
Finally, the ruling of POW's, the Islamic ruling on POW's.

357
00:26:45,581 --> 00:26:51,554
It is up to the leader, it is up to the Muslim Imam(امام) to determine the fate of POW's.

358
00:26:52,070 --> 00:26:54,212
He has the choice of executing them,

359
00:26:55,487 --> 00:26:58,548
example is Uqba Bin Abi Moait(عقبة بن أبي معيط) and An-Nadhar Bin Hariss(ألنضر بن حارث),

360
00:26:58,643 --> 00:27:00,929
who were executed by Rasool Allah ﷺ.

361
00:27:01,803 --> 00:27:02,699
Number two,

362
00:27:03,246 --> 00:27:07,414
 He can free them without ransom as he did with Abu Izza(ابوعزة) and Abul Aas(ابوالعاص),

363
00:27:08,277 --> 00:27:14,460
he can free them with ransom, like he did with the rest of the POW's.

364
00:27:14,959 --> 00:27:18,600
And he has the option of enslaving the POW's

365
00:27:19,080 --> 00:27:23,282
such as the ruling of Saad Bin Muadh(سعد بن معاذ) on Bannu Quraidha(بنو قريظة),

366
00:27:23,475 --> 00:27:24,985
as we'll talk about later on.

367
00:27:25,897 --> 00:27:29,713
So these are the rulings of POW's in Islam.

368
00:27:29,776 --> 00:27:35,744
We have our own Geneva Convention, we don't have to abide by anyone's Geneva Convention.

369
00:27:35,784 --> 00:27:40,300
Allahعَزّوجَلّ has already taught us, what is right and what is wrong.

370
00:27:40,713 --> 00:27:48,002
So Muslims have their own rules which are part of the Sharia(شريعة) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

371
00:27:48,319 --> 00:27:53,307
and it has the Hidaya(هداية) that Muslims would need,

372
00:27:53,545 --> 00:27:54,905
 فِيْهِ اَلْهُدَى

373
00:27:56,966 --> 00:28:03,359
Usaid Bin Khuzair رضي الله عنه, he came to Rasool Allah ﷺ, after the Battle of Badr(بدر) and he said;

374
00:28:03,450 --> 00:28:09,041
 O Messenger of Allah, We didn't know that any fighting would have occurred otherwise we would have followed you,

375
00:28:09,347 --> 00:28:12,022
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him, You are speaking the truth.

376
00:28:12,993 --> 00:28:15,850
So, some of Al-Ansaar(الأنْصَار), who stayed behind.

377
00:28:16,120 --> 00:28:18,858
They stayed behind, not because they didn't want to fight

378
00:28:18,898 --> 00:28:22,064
but because they didn't think that fighting would happen.

379
00:28:22,363 --> 00:28:29,927
Because we said that the original intent of the army, was to raid the caravan and not to meet an army.

380
00:28:31,266 --> 00:28:33,181
What is the status of the people of Badr(بدر)?

381
00:28:34,483 --> 00:28:37,734
Well the people of Badr(بدر) carry a special status.

382
00:28:39,056 --> 00:28:41,618
Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and asked him,

383
00:28:42,043 --> 00:28:44,487
 مَا تَعُدُّوْنَ اَهْلَ بَدْرٍ فِيْكُمْ

384
00:28:45,343 --> 00:28:48,074
What do you consider the people of Badr(بدر) among you to be.?

385
00:28:48,114 --> 00:28:50,311
 What is the status of the people of Badr(بدر) among you?

386
00:28:50,966 --> 00:28:54,549
Rasool Allah ﷺ said; They are among the best of the Muslims.

387
00:28:54,748 --> 00:29:00,440
 Jibreel(جِبْرِيْل) said; the same is the case with the angels, who attended Badr(بدر).

388
00:29:01,717 --> 00:29:04,902
So, Badr(بدر) wasn't a special event for the Muslims, who attended it,

389
00:29:04,971 --> 00:29:08,503
but it was also a special event for the angels who attended it.

390
00:29:08,915 --> 00:29:11,844
The Muslims who attended Badr(بدر) are the best of Muslims

391
00:29:11,901 --> 00:29:14,965
and the angels who attended Badr(بدر) are the best of angels.

392
00:29:15,814 --> 00:29:21,016
And that's why, in our books the people of Badr(بدر) are considered to be a special class,

393
00:29:21,041 --> 00:29:22,867
you know Tabaqat-Al-Badriyeen(طبقة البدرين),

394
00:29:23,111 --> 00:29:25,790
the class of the people of Badr(بدر), they are special class.

395
00:29:27,333 --> 00:29:31,558
When Hatib Ibn Abi Baltaa(حاطب بن أبي بلتعة) committed an act of treason,

396
00:29:32,880 --> 00:29:34,524
against Allah and His Messenger,

397
00:29:35,548 --> 00:29:40,651
by informing the people of Makkah of the plans of Rasool Allah ﷺ to attack them.

398
00:29:41,741 --> 00:29:44,283
Umar Bin Khattab(عمر بن خطاب) came to Rasool Allah ﷺ and said;

399
00:29:44,323 --> 00:29:46,950
O Messenger of Allah, Let me execute him.

400
00:29:47,243 --> 00:29:48,378
He is a Munafiq(منافق).

401
00:29:48,843 --> 00:29:56,909
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: O Umar(عُمَر), Probably Allah has looked down at the people of Badr(بدر) and said;

402
00:29:57,044 --> 00:29:59,981
 Do whatever you want because I have forgiven you

403
00:30:01,643 --> 00:30:07,190
Rasool Allah ﷺ is saying that the people of Badr(بدر), because of attending Badr(بدر),

404
00:30:07,875 --> 00:30:14,313
Allah looked at them and said, You can now, do whatever you want,

405
00:30:14,763 --> 00:30:16,159
because I have forgiven you.

406
00:30:16,632 --> 00:30:21,268
When Rasool Allah ﷺ said that, the eyes of Umar(عُمَر) swelled with tears.

407
00:30:22,808 --> 00:30:26,394
Hatib Bin Abi Baltaa(حاطب بن أبي بلتعة), was one of the Muslims, who attended Badr(بدر).

408
00:30:26,912 --> 00:30:31,207
And because of that, Allahعَزّوجَلّ has granted them forgiveness.

409
00:30:31,247 --> 00:30:33,326
 Rasool Allah ﷺ says in another Hadith(حديث),

410
00:30:33,917 --> 00:30:37,977
No one who attended Badr(بدر) or Hudaybiyah(حديبية) will enter into Hell fire.

411
00:30:39,179 --> 00:30:40,866
So, the people of Badr(بدر) are special.

412
00:30:41,413 --> 00:30:45,034
 Some of the consequences of the Battle of Badr(بدر).

413
00:30:46,833 --> 00:30:48,732
Number one, hypocrisy.

414
00:30:49,548 --> 00:30:55,615
There were many people in Madina, who were not happy to see the Muslims victorious.

415
00:30:57,056 --> 00:31:00,098
But they're not strong enough to publicly declare that.

416
00:31:00,724 --> 00:31:02,024
So, they went underground.

417
00:31:03,364 --> 00:31:05,213
They publicly professed Islam.

418
00:31:06,217 --> 00:31:09,460
Outwardly you can't tell the difference between them and the Muslims.

419
00:31:10,325 --> 00:31:15,208
They pray like Muslims, they fast like Muslims, they pay Zakah(زكواة) like Muslims.

420
00:31:16,438 --> 00:31:20,469
They attend the gatherings of Muslims, they attend the lessons of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

421
00:31:21,258 --> 00:31:24,966
But deep in their hearts, they despised Islam.

422
00:31:25,374 --> 00:31:32,321
They hate the Muslims, and they wish that Islam would vanish from the face of the earth.

423
00:31:32,983 --> 00:31:35,593
They wish that Islam did not come to Madina.

424
00:31:37,077 --> 00:31:38,757
And these were Al-Munafiqoon(ألمنافقون),

425
00:31:39,739 --> 00:31:45,560
But because Islam was now victorious, and the Muslims were strong,

426
00:31:46,207 --> 00:31:50,030
and the power of Rasool Allah ﷺ in Madina was increasing,

427
00:31:50,497 --> 00:31:53,572
they dared not speak their minds.

428
00:31:55,005 --> 00:31:56,760
So, they were jumping the bandwagon.

429
00:31:58,181 --> 00:32:04,214
And they were plotting underground against the Muslims.

430
00:32:05,277 --> 00:32:08,287
And the hypocrites were an extremely dangerous enemy,

431
00:32:08,311 --> 00:32:11,371
we could probably say that they're the most dangerous enemy of all,

432
00:32:11,600 --> 00:32:16,826
because they were living with the Muslims, and they knew the secrets of the Muslims.

433
00:32:17,223 --> 00:32:23,586
And they were passing on these secrets to the outside enemies of Islam.

434
00:32:24,669 --> 00:32:25,867
So they were a fifth column.

435
00:32:26,870 --> 00:32:29,993
These were the ones, who're delivering the news to Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

436
00:32:30,660 --> 00:32:37,988
these were the ones, who were assisting the enemies of Allah, in their planning against the messenger of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

437
00:32:38,647 --> 00:32:40,435
So, it was a very dangerous situation,

438
00:32:40,703 --> 00:32:42,922
and it's a very difficult enemy to deal with.

439
00:32:43,247 --> 00:32:50,069
Because they don't go public with their disbelief,

440
00:32:50,958 --> 00:32:55,234
and they are blending perfectly among the Muslim community.

441
00:32:56,163 --> 00:33:00,045
Rasool Allah ﷺ himself didn't know about many of these hypocrites.

442
00:33:00,165 --> 00:33:03,933
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says; You don't know them, we know them.

443
00:33:04,783 --> 00:33:08,681
So, even Rasool Allah ﷺ did not know the names of some of these Munafiqeen(منافقين),

444
00:33:08,705 --> 00:33:11,848
until later on, when they were revealed to him by Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

445
00:33:12,779 --> 00:33:14,126
Allahسبحانه تعالى says about them;

446
00:33:14,476 --> 00:33:21,721
وَإِذَا لَقُوا الَّذِينَ آمَنُوا قَالُوا آمَنَّا

447
00:33:22,110 --> 00:33:33,330
وَإِذَا خَلَوْا إِلَىٰ شَيَاطِينِهِمْ قَالُوا إِنَّا مَعَكُمْ إِنَّمَا نَحْنُ مُسْتَهْزِئُونَ۝

448
00:33:34,289 --> 00:33:37,882
When they meet those who believe they say we believe,

449
00:33:38,268 --> 00:33:40,693
but when they are alone with their evil ones,

450
00:33:40,859 --> 00:33:45,485
they say indeed we are with you, we were only mockers.

451
00:33:46,272 --> 00:33:49,344
So, when they're with the Muslims, they say we are like you, we are Muslim.

452
00:33:50,233 --> 00:33:52,693
So, this was a consequence of the Battle of Badr(بدر)

453
00:33:52,774 --> 00:33:57,823
that now you have this new category of people Al-Munafiqoon(ألمنافقون),

454
00:33:57,922 --> 00:34:00,585
before you had kuffar(كفار) and Muslims,

455
00:34:00,672 --> 00:34:04,114
now you have Kuffar(كفار) Munafiqoon(منافقون) and Muslims,

456
00:34:04,199 --> 00:34:09,139
now Munafiqoon(منافقون) are part of Kuffar(كفار), but the difference is that they claim to be Muslim.

457
00:34:11,173 --> 00:34:14,810
Umair Ibn Wahb(عمير إبن وهب) was one of the devil's of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

458
00:34:15,227 --> 00:34:19,214
He was sitting with Safwaan Ibn Ummayyah(صفوان إبن اُمَيَّة) next to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

459
00:34:20,435 --> 00:34:27,398
And he said, If it wasn't for the fact that I'm in debt, and I have children to care for

460
00:34:28,486 --> 00:34:31,049
I would go and assassinate Muhammad(محمد) myself.

461
00:34:32,446 --> 00:34:34,877
So, Safwaan(صفوان) took advantage of that and he said,

462
00:34:36,000 --> 00:34:40,653
I will pay your debt and I'll take care of your children, if anything happens to you.

463
00:34:41,912 --> 00:34:46,216
So, Umair Ibn Wahb(عمير إبن وهب) agreed with Safwaan(صفوان), that he will travel to Madina,

464
00:34:46,815 --> 00:34:53,403
with the intent of assassinating Rasool Allah ﷺ.

465
00:34:54,704 --> 00:35:01,484
So he dips his sword and poison, until it absorbs, the poison

466
00:35:02,159 --> 00:35:05,417
 and then he rushes towards Madina.

467
00:35:07,187 --> 00:35:13,562
He enters Madina and he passes next to a gathering that included Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب).

468
00:35:14,609 --> 00:35:17,641
Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) was talking to some men, about the Battle of Badr(بدر).

469
00:35:18,097 --> 00:35:19,712
He was talking to people who didn't attend it.

470
00:35:20,780 --> 00:35:22,724
You know Badr(بدر) was all, what they were talking about.

471
00:35:23,548 --> 00:35:25,595
A great victory, everyone is happy.

472
00:35:26,301 --> 00:35:29,508
They are narrating all of the stories of what went on.

473
00:35:30,574 --> 00:35:33,640
So, Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) spots Umair Ibn Wahb(عمير إبن وهب) and he said,

474
00:35:34,237 --> 00:35:40,664
this enemy of Allah, This dog, Umair Ibn Wahb(عمير إبن وهب) is not here for any good.

475
00:35:42,066 --> 00:35:45,037
And he stands up and he grabs Umair Ibn Wahb(عمير إبن وهب)

476
00:35:45,428 --> 00:35:48,804
and he wraps the sheath of his sword around his neck.

477
00:35:51,078 --> 00:35:55,316
And then he takes him to Rasool Allah ﷺ,

478
00:35:55,356 --> 00:35:58,771
he says, O Messenger of Allah, this enemy of Allah did not come for any good.

479
00:35:58,811 --> 00:36:02,033
Rasool Allah ﷺ said, Let him go Umar(عُمَر), release him.

480
00:36:02,687 --> 00:36:04,537
So, he was released by Umar(عُمَر).

481
00:36:04,684 --> 00:36:11,104
But then Umar(عُمَر) told some of the Sahabah outside, Be careful, and guard Rasool Allah ﷺ,

482
00:36:12,905 --> 00:36:15,556
 so Umair Ibn Wahb(عمير إبن وهب) comes in and he said;

483
00:36:15,768 --> 00:36:17,056
عمت صباحا

484
00:36:17,112 --> 00:36:18,112
Good Morning

485
00:36:19,030 --> 00:36:23,917
Rasool Allah ﷺ said: Allah has replaced us with a better greeting than that

486
00:36:24,274 --> 00:36:25,837
اَلسلام عليكم ورحمة الله

487
00:36:26,562 --> 00:36:30,496
Umair Ibn Wahb(عمير إبن وهب) said, you haven't been using that for long,

488
00:36:31,051 --> 00:36:35,315
meaning that, you just changed your tradition and your customs.

489
00:36:35,827 --> 00:36:38,504
Otherwise before, you used to say good morning just like us.

490
00:36:40,311 --> 00:36:42,655
Anyway, Rasool Allah ﷺ told him: Why did you come?

491
00:36:42,761 --> 00:36:46,941
He said: I came to ask for the release of my son.

492
00:36:47,393 --> 00:36:53,071
His son Wahb(وهب) was a POW, that was his cover story.

493
00:36:53,984 --> 00:36:57,317
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him, Tell me the truth. Why did you come?

494
00:36:57,987 --> 00:37:02,537
He said; that's why, I came, I came to ask for the release of my son.

495
00:37:03,148 --> 00:37:06,828
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him; So why are you carrying a sword?

496
00:37:07,569 --> 00:37:07,873
He said;

497
00:37:07,953 --> 00:37:10,448
تَبَّتْ الَّهَا مِنْ سُيُوْفُهَا الْاَغْنَتْ عَنَّا شَيْاً

498
00:37:10,694 --> 00:37:14,099
Woe to these swords, they haven't done us any good.

499
00:37:15,778 --> 00:37:17,659
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him; You are lying.

500
00:37:18,564 --> 00:37:22,375
The reason, why you came is because you met with Safwaan(صفوان) next to Al-Ka'aba(اَلْكَعْبَه).

501
00:37:23,026 --> 00:37:23,843
And you told him

502
00:37:23,970 --> 00:37:27,866
that if it wasn't for the fact that you are in debt, and you have children to take care of,

503
00:37:29,229 --> 00:37:30,881
you would come and assassinate me.

504
00:37:31,905 --> 00:37:33,713
And then Safwaan(صفوان) told you,

505
00:37:34,518 --> 00:37:38,003
I will take care of your debt and your children, If anything happens to you.

506
00:37:38,866 --> 00:37:44,071
And then you agreed with Safwaan(صفوان) that you will keep, this issue secret and you'll tell nobody about it.

507
00:37:45,273 --> 00:37:45,984
Umair(عمير) said:

508
00:37:46,064 --> 00:37:47,841
 اَشْهَدُ اَنَّكَ رَسُوْلُ الله

509
00:37:48,690 --> 00:37:51,726
I testify that you are the messenger of Allah

510
00:37:51,766 --> 00:37:56,750
because no one overheard that conversation between me and Safwaan(صفوان).

511
00:37:57,972 --> 00:38:01,439
So only Allahعَزّوجَلّ could tell you about that conversation

512
00:38:02,206 --> 00:38:03,772
and he became Muslim.

513
00:38:04,375 --> 00:38:09,683
And he goes back to Makkah, and on his way back, Safwaan(صفوان) was telling the people of Makkah,

514
00:38:10,938 --> 00:38:15,852
soon you will hear news that will make you forget what happened in Badr(بدر).

515
00:38:16,852 --> 00:38:20,176
 He would go around telling them, soon the good news will come.

516
00:38:20,713 --> 00:38:23,165
You're going to hear some good news, it's on its way.

517
00:38:23,885 --> 00:38:27,861
But then Umair Ibn Wahb(عمير إبن وهب) comes back declaring Islam.

518
00:38:28,886 --> 00:38:31,323
Safwaan(صفوان) said: I'm never going to speak to him again.

519
00:38:32,446 --> 00:38:36,473
Now, Umair Ibn Wahb(عمير إبن وهب), who was a devil of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ) now becomes a Daiyah(داعيه),

520
00:38:37,355 --> 00:38:41,077
and instead of persecuting Muslims as he used to do,

521
00:38:41,424 --> 00:38:44,305
he would persecute the people, who would persecute Muslims.

522
00:38:45,329 --> 00:38:49,922
And many people became Muslim through the Da'wah(دعوة) of Umair Ibn Wahb(عمير إبن وهب), Allah Ho Akbar(الله اكبر).

523
00:38:52,033 --> 00:38:54,263
Some lessons from the Battle of Badr(بدر).

524
00:38:55,072 --> 00:38:58,727
Number one, victory is from Allah,

525
00:38:59,712 --> 00:39:12,720
after victory, normally, soldiers will be very proud of their training, their skill, their bravery.

526
00:39:13,436 --> 00:39:19,786
Allahعَزّوجَلّ never ever praised the Muslims for their victory, never.

527
00:39:20,909 --> 00:39:25,853
Look at the Ayaat(آيات) that commented on the victory of Muslims.

528
00:39:26,123 --> 00:39:27,449
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

529
00:39:27,715 --> 00:39:35,785
وَمَا جَعَلَهُ اللَّهُ إِلَّا بُشْرَىٰ لَكُمْ وَلِتَطْمَئِنَّ قُلُوبُكُمْ بِهِ ۗ

530
00:39:36,031 --> 00:39:43,661
وَمَا النَّصْرُ إِلَّا مِنْ عِنْدِ اللَّهِ الْعَزِيزِ الْحَكِيمِ۝

531
00:39:44,407 --> 00:39:49,615
And victory is not except from Allah, the Exalted in Might and Wise.

532
00:39:50,927 --> 00:39:52,194
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ says;

533
00:39:52,582 --> 00:39:57,766
فَلَمْ تَقْتُلُوهُمْ وَلَٰكِنَّ اللَّهَ قَتَلَهُمْ ۚ

534
00:39:57,933 --> 00:40:03,845
وَمَا رَمَيْتَ إِذْ رَمَيْتَ وَلَٰكِنَّ اللَّهَ رَمَىٰ ۚ

535
00:40:04,301 --> 00:40:07,314
And you did not kill them, but it was Allah, who kill them

536
00:40:07,782 --> 00:40:13,287
And You threw not, O Muhammad(محمد) when you threw, but it was Allah, who threw,

537
00:40:13,756 --> 00:40:16,314
that He might test the believers with a good test.

538
00:40:17,060 --> 00:40:19,459
So, who does the credit go to.? Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

539
00:40:20,915 --> 00:40:25,673
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ is dealing with the aftermath of victory,

540
00:40:26,637 --> 00:40:32,380
He is dealing with the potential of or the probability of Muslims feeling pride

541
00:40:33,760 --> 00:40:38,819
and having confidence in their abilities or attributing the victory to their abilities.

542
00:40:38,843 --> 00:40:44,398
Allahعَزّوجَلّ is telling them, the victory was a blessing from Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

543
00:40:44,689 --> 00:40:48,341
It came from Allahعَزّوجَلّ, it was Allahعَزّوجَلّ, Who gave you that victory?

544
00:40:50,111 --> 00:40:54,804
And for example, when the Muslims came to congratulate Rasool Allah ﷺ,

545
00:40:54,844 --> 00:40:57,718
so one of those Sahabah responded back by saying,

546
00:40:57,949 --> 00:41:01,328
Why are you congratulating us? What are you congratulating us for?

547
00:41:01,717 --> 00:41:03,703
إن لَقينا إلا عجائزَ صُلعًا

548
00:41:04,007 --> 00:41:10,655
We have only met old bald men, like camels waiting for slaughter and we slaughtered them.

549
00:41:11,600 --> 00:41:14,475
So, he's like saying, it was so easy,

550
00:41:15,003 --> 00:41:20,473
Rasool Allah ﷺ told him; Don't say that, O, cousin, Those were the leaders.

551
00:41:21,517 --> 00:41:23,024
It was Allah, Who made it easy.

552
00:41:23,552 --> 00:41:27,154
This was a formidable foe, it was a strong foe,

553
00:41:27,781 --> 00:41:30,187
don't belittle their ability and strength.

554
00:41:31,031 --> 00:41:36,138
But the victory that you achieved was because Allahعَزّوجَلّ made it easy for you.

555
00:41:36,864 --> 00:41:38,204
So, this is very important,

556
00:41:38,812 --> 00:41:44,125
that whatever victory we achieve in any avenue of life,

557
00:41:44,627 --> 00:41:47,975
we attribute it to the one, it belongs to, and that is Allahعَزّوجَلّ,

558
00:41:49,554 --> 00:41:51,702
whether you are successful in your business,

559
00:41:52,230 --> 00:41:54,633
whether you are successful in your education,

560
00:41:55,337 --> 00:41:58,387
whether you are successful with your family,

561
00:41:58,990 --> 00:42:01,037
whether you are successful as a Daiyah(داعيه),

562
00:42:01,688 --> 00:42:04,292
whether you are successful as an Imam(امام), or scholar,

563
00:42:04,803 --> 00:42:07,479
attribute it, to the one it belongs to and that is Allah.

564
00:42:08,338 --> 00:42:10,054
Don't be like Qaroon(قارون), who said;

565
00:42:10,379 --> 00:42:12,636
 إِنَّمَا أُوتِيتُهُ عَلَىٰ عِلْمٍ عِنْدِي ۚ

566
00:42:12,933 --> 00:42:16,522
I have this wealth because of my skill, because of my knowledge.

567
00:42:18,065 --> 00:42:19,255
That's the first lesson.

568
00:42:20,112 --> 00:42:23,130
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says, in another Ayah(آية) that I forgot to mention,

569
00:42:23,397 --> 00:42:34,922
وَاذْكُرُوا إِذْ أَنْتُمْ قَلِيلٌ مُسْتَضْعَفُونَ فِي الْأَرْضِ تَخَافُونَ أَنْ يَتَخَطَّفَكُمُ النَّاسُ

570
00:42:35,350 --> 00:42:45,815
فَآوَاكُمْ وَأَيَّدَكُمْ بِنَصْرِهِ وَرَزَقَكُمْ مِنَ الطَّيِّبَاتِ لَعَلَّكُمْ تَشْكُرُونَ۝

571
00:42:46,251 --> 00:42:52,048
And remember when you were few and oppressed in the land fearing that people might abduct you.

572
00:42:52,175 --> 00:42:55,342
 That is who, you were, you were few, you were oppressed

573
00:42:55,652 --> 00:42:58,969
 and you used to fear that people might abduct you, but He sheltered you

574
00:42:59,617 --> 00:43:05,249
supported you with His victory, and provided you with good things that you might be grateful.

575
00:43:06,463 --> 00:43:09,539
Some of the miracles, that occurred in Badr(بدر).

576
00:43:10,027 --> 00:43:13,019
The reducing of numbers insight, we talked about that.

577
00:43:14,101 --> 00:43:16,426
The rain, the sleep,

578
00:43:17,005 --> 00:43:19,815
they slept very well, the night before the battle.

579
00:43:20,291 --> 00:43:21,854
The angels coming down.

580
00:43:23,039 --> 00:43:24,647
Ummayyah Bin Khalaf(اُمَيَّة بن خلف)

581
00:43:25,227 --> 00:43:31,217
because Rasool Allah ﷺ said that he will be killed and his prophecy was fulfilled.

582
00:43:32,202 --> 00:43:34,350
The Sword of Ukasha(عكاشه),

583
00:43:34,779 --> 00:43:41,640
he had the wooden sword and Rasool Allah ﷺ held it and it turns into a real sword, that's another miracle.

584
00:43:42,537 --> 00:43:46,834
The killing of the Imams(اِمَام) of Kuffr(كفر), that's a miracle because before the Battle, Rasool Allah ﷺ said;

585
00:43:47,049 --> 00:43:50,594
this is where so and so will be killed, this is where so and so will be killed,

586
00:43:50,877 --> 00:43:52,556
 this is where so and so will be killed,

587
00:43:52,596 --> 00:43:57,027
and they were killed exactly in the spots that were pointed by Rasool Allah ﷺ.

588
00:43:57,747 --> 00:43:58,885
The Eye of Qatadah(قتاده).

589
00:43:59,107 --> 00:44:04,956
Qatada(قتاده), had one of his eyes fall out of its socket and it was only hanging by the nerve.

590
00:44:05,531 --> 00:44:08,020
And they were about to cut it.

591
00:44:08,858 --> 00:44:11,752
When Rasool Allah ﷺ told them not to do so.

592
00:44:12,029 --> 00:44:17,676
And then Rasool Allah ﷺ held the eye, placed it back in its socket, and then wiped it.

593
00:44:19,159 --> 00:44:23,927
Qatada(قتاده), would say that that eye became stronger than my other eye.

594
00:44:25,153 --> 00:44:27,258
That's a miracle of Rasool Allah ﷺ.

595
00:44:27,535 --> 00:44:31,183
Knowing the whereabouts of the money of Al-Abbas(العباس).

596
00:44:31,782 --> 00:44:36,255
Revealing the assassination plot that Wahb Ibn Umair(عمير إبن وهب) was planning.

597
00:44:37,413 --> 00:44:39,261
All of these are miracles that happened in Badr(بدر),

598
00:44:39,301 --> 00:44:43,649
so you can see that yes, Qur'an is the greatest miracle of Rasool Allah ﷺ,

599
00:44:43,689 --> 00:44:48,359
but he had so many physical miracles, many more than probably any other Prophet.

600
00:44:49,705 --> 00:44:51,992
A word on the miracles of Rasool Allah ﷺ

601
00:44:52,032 --> 00:44:55,794
and I think I spoke about this, in some of my other talks.

602
00:44:56,296 --> 00:45:00,942
Most of the miracles of Rasool Allah ﷺ occurred in the context of Jihad(جهاد).

603
00:45:01,767 --> 00:45:08,057
And also most of the karmaat(كرامات) of the Auliyaa(أوليآء) of Allahعَزّوجَلّ occur in the context of Jihad(جهاد).

604
00:45:08,824 --> 00:45:11,707
So really, jihad(جهاد) is where the Karamaat(كرامات) happen.

605
00:45:13,029 --> 00:45:15,986
The next lesson Wala'a and Bara'a(ألولآء ولبرآء),

606
00:45:16,447 --> 00:45:21,475
Loyalty to Allah and His Messenger and the believers,

607
00:45:21,904 --> 00:45:25,888
and disassociating oneself from disbelief.

608
00:45:26,793 --> 00:45:28,348
Few examples from Badr(بدر).

609
00:45:28,896 --> 00:45:35,282
Abu Bakr(ابوبكر) was on the Muslim side and his son was on the side of Al-Kuffar(ألكفار), his son Abdur Rahman(عبدالرحمن).

610
00:45:36,986 --> 00:45:39,118
Abdur Rahman Ibn Abu Bakr(عبدالرحمن ابن ابوبكر) said,

611
00:45:39,373 --> 00:45:42,082
he told his father later on, when he became Muslim, he said;

612
00:45:42,969 --> 00:45:48,829
O, my father, I saw you on the day of Badr(بدر)

613
00:45:49,388 --> 00:45:50,937
but I would avoid you.

614
00:45:51,716 --> 00:45:54,139
Because I didn't want to attack you.

615
00:45:55,798 --> 00:45:56,778
Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) said;

616
00:45:56,897 --> 00:46:01,274
 I didn't see you and If I saw you, I would have pursued you and killed you.

617
00:46:02,278 --> 00:46:09,211
So, Abu Bakr(ابو بكر) was willing to fight his own son, for the sake of Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

618
00:46:10,652 --> 00:46:12,680
We talked about the story of Abu Hudaifah(ابوحذيفه)

619
00:46:13,129 --> 00:46:18,494
and his father Utba(عتبة), when he saw that his father was buried in Al-Qulaib(ألقليب).

620
00:46:19,340 --> 00:46:24,203
Mus'ab Ibn Umair(مصعب إبن عمير) and his brother Abu Aziz(ابوعزيز), who was a POW

621
00:46:25,048 --> 00:46:30,333
Mus'ab(مصعب) passed by the Ansaar(أنْصَار), who were holding Abu Aziz(ابوعزيز)

622
00:46:31,129 --> 00:46:38,459
and he told them, tie his hands fast, tighten the ropes, on Abu Aziz(ابوعزيز),

623
00:46:39,074 --> 00:46:42,501
because his mother is wealthy, and she'll ransom him for you.

624
00:46:43,029 --> 00:46:44,331
So, Subhaan Allah(سُبْحَان الله),

625
00:46:44,592 --> 00:46:49,915
Is this an advice that Mus'ab(مصعب) should give, to the ones who are holding his brother?

626
00:46:51,531 --> 00:46:56,639
Hold him well tighten the ropes that are tying him because his mother will ransom him.

627
00:46:56,932 --> 00:47:00,934
So, his brother was amazed, his brother said; Brother, Is this how you treat me?

628
00:47:01,840 --> 00:47:05,909
Mus'ab Ibn Umair(مصعب إبن عمير) said, He's more my brother than you are.

629
00:47:06,421 --> 00:47:08,549
He was pointing to the men who are holding him,

630
00:47:08,589 --> 00:47:11,208
he was pointing to the Ansaar(أنْصَار), who are holding him and he said,

631
00:47:11,574 --> 00:47:13,913
these are my real brothers, you are not.

632
00:47:15,006 --> 00:47:17,259
These are my brothers, because of Islam.

633
00:47:18,484 --> 00:47:23,386
And even though you are my blood brother, but your Kuffr(كفر) has separated between us.

634
00:47:25,513 --> 00:47:27,870
Another issue relating to Wala'a and Bara'a(ألولآء ولبرآء).

635
00:47:29,057 --> 00:47:32,012
There were some of the young men of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ),

636
00:47:32,778 --> 00:47:36,462
who were interested in Islam and actually did become Muslim.

637
00:47:37,406 --> 00:47:42,565
And these were sons of some of the noble families of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

638
00:47:43,907 --> 00:47:48,430
Allah Ho Alam(الله اعلم) did they become Muslim, because they sincerely believed in Islam,

639
00:47:48,470 --> 00:47:56,413
 or they become Muslim because it was a revolt against the status quo, and they're just interested in it as a fad.

640
00:47:56,872 --> 00:47:59,583
Like we will see among some of the youth of today,

641
00:47:59,623 --> 00:48:03,118
they just want to embrace some things because they're different, I mean, it makes them different.

642
00:48:03,846 --> 00:48:07,700
So these were wealthy young kids in Makkah, and they became Muslim,

643
00:48:08,723 --> 00:48:12,469
such as Ali Bin Ummayyah Bin Khalaf(علي بن أميه بن خلف)

644
00:48:13,334 --> 00:48:15,797
and Abul Qais Bin Al-Waleed Bin Mugheera(ابو القيس بن وليد بن مغيره),

645
00:48:16,464 --> 00:48:18,360
and Abul Qais Bin Fakeh(ابو القيس بن فاكه),

646
00:48:18,783 --> 00:48:22,354
and Al-Haris Bin Zama'a(ألحارث بن زمعة), and Al-Aas Bin Munnabbah(ألعاص بن منبه).

647
00:48:22,507 --> 00:48:25,971
These were all sons of the wealthy men of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

648
00:48:26,912 --> 00:48:33,507
They became Muslim, but they couldn't withstand the demands of Islam,

649
00:48:33,769 --> 00:48:37,158
the sacrifice that the slam asks from you.

650
00:48:38,026 --> 00:48:41,071
So they stayed behind them, they didn't make Hijrah(هجرة), they weren't willing.

651
00:48:41,200 --> 00:48:47,152
These are spoiled kids, they weren't willing to go through the hassle of Hijrah(هجرة) and all of that,

652
00:48:47,414 --> 00:48:54,347
 you know will be Muslim if it's convenient, but if it's gonna cost us too much, then forget about it.

653
00:48:55,272 --> 00:48:56,580
So, they stayed behind.

654
00:48:56,950 --> 00:49:04,299
And in fact, they joined with their fathers and their tribe in the Battle of Badr(بدر).

655
00:49:06,097 --> 00:49:11,121
Ibn Hishaam(ابن هشام) says, All of them were killed on the Battle of Badr(بدر).

656
00:49:13,453 --> 00:49:16,479
So, the Muslim said, Well, you know, these were Muslim.

657
00:49:17,126 --> 00:49:20,531
Probably they don't want to go out and fight and they're Muslim.

658
00:49:21,496 --> 00:49:25,732
So, Allahعَزّوجَلّ revealed. Verse 97. of Surat-Un-Nissa(سورة النساء),

659
00:49:27,113 --> 00:49:28,332
talking about them,

660
00:49:29,530 --> 00:49:38,767
إِنَّ الَّذِينَ تَوَفَّاهُمُ الْمَلَائِكَةُ ظَالِمِي أَنْفُسِهِمْ

661
00:49:39,188 --> 00:49:46,084
قَالُوا فِيمَ كُنْتُمْ ۖ قَالُوا كُنَّا مُسْتَضْعَفِينَ فِي الْأَرْضِ ۚ

662
00:49:46,608 --> 00:49:55,024
قَالُوا أَلَمْ تَكُنْ أَرْضُ اللَّهِ وَاسِعَةً فَتُهَاجِرُوا فِيهَا ۚ

663
00:49:55,492 --> 00:50:04,815
فَأُولَٰئِكَ مَأْوَاهُمْ جَهَنَّمُ ۖ وَسَاءَتْ مَصِيرًا۝

664
00:50:05,936 --> 00:50:08,279
I want you, the listener to think about this.

665
00:50:08,319 --> 00:50:09,747
What do you think their fate is?

666
00:50:10,586 --> 00:50:12,955
They were Muslim,

667
00:50:13,944 --> 00:50:18,398
But they didn't go far enough, in sacrificing for Islam,

668
00:50:18,422 --> 00:50:21,594
they stayed behind and then they ended up being killed in the Battle of Badr(بدر).

669
00:50:22,335 --> 00:50:25,028
Probably they've never shot an arrow

670
00:50:25,675 --> 00:50:28,157
probably they never struck with a sword.

671
00:50:28,208 --> 00:50:30,644
They just went out in the army because they had to,

672
00:50:31,327 --> 00:50:33,255
you know, a soldier is called to duty.

673
00:50:34,710 --> 00:50:36,470
What do you think their fate was?

674
00:50:37,123 --> 00:50:38,723
Allahعَزّوجَلّ said;

675
00:50:39,399 --> 00:50:45,133
Indeed, those whom the angels take in death while wronging themselves,

676
00:50:45,284 --> 00:50:49,002
 the angels will say, in what condition were you?

677
00:50:49,303 --> 00:50:52,419
 They will say; we were oppressed in the land.

678
00:50:52,946 --> 00:50:54,823
They, the angels will say,

679
00:50:55,115 --> 00:50:59,350
was not the earth of Allah spacious enough for you to immigrate therein.?

680
00:50:59,839 --> 00:51:01,926
For those, their refuge is hell

681
00:51:02,533 --> 00:51:05,236
and evil it is as a destination.

682
00:51:06,835 --> 00:51:10,179
So, don't play around with Islam.

683
00:51:10,712 --> 00:51:12,191
Don't fool around with it.

684
00:51:12,866 --> 00:51:14,445
This is a serious religion.

685
00:51:14,842 --> 00:51:16,501
And you need to be serious.

686
00:51:17,064 --> 00:51:18,442
Allahعَزّوجَلّ says in Qur'an,

687
00:51:18,475 --> 00:51:20,307
يَا يَحْيَىٰ خُذِ الْكِتَابَ بِقُوَّةٍ ۖ

688
00:51:20,347 --> 00:51:24,545
O Yahya(يحيى) hold the book with strength, hold it strong.

689
00:51:25,474 --> 00:51:27,836
And Allahعَزّوجَلّ tells Banni Israel(بني إسرائيل),

690
00:51:28,878 --> 00:51:31,013
خُذُوا مَا آتَيْنَاكُم بِقُوَّةٍ

691
00:51:31,263 --> 00:51:33,561
Hold fast, what we have given you.

692
00:51:34,347 --> 00:51:38,093
So, this religion does not accept half hearted effort

693
00:51:38,173 --> 00:51:43,855
and giving it part time, or being a Muslim when it's convenient.

694
00:51:44,382 --> 00:51:46,853
And doing otherwise when it's not.

695
00:51:47,459 --> 00:51:50,843
Allahعَزّوجَلّ has promised you Jannah(جنة) but you have to pay a price.

696
00:51:51,809 --> 00:51:54,351
In the Tafseer(تفسير) of this Ayyah(آية) by Ibn Kathir(إبن كثير).

697
00:51:55,495 --> 00:51:58,370
He mentions a few narrations. One of them is by Bukhari(بخاريْ),

698
00:51:59,552 --> 00:52:04,725
It says that Ibn Abbas(إبن عباس) said: that this Ayah(آية) is talking about some Muslims

699
00:52:05,350 --> 00:52:09,636
who were with the disbelievers adding to their numbers,

700
00:52:09,716 --> 00:52:13,310
meaning that they didn't really go out to fight, they just went because they had to.

701
00:52:13,350 --> 00:52:16,505
A soldier responding to the call of duty, they had to go out.

702
00:52:17,952 --> 00:52:22,497
يَاْتِي السَّهَمْ يَرْمِيْ بِهِ فَيُصِيْب اَحَدُهُمْ فَيَقْتُلُ اَوْ يَضْرِبْ عُنُقُهُ فَيُقْتَلْ

703
00:52:22,576 --> 00:52:26,452
And while they're in the army, an arrow would come and kill one of them

704
00:52:26,492 --> 00:52:28,735
 and a blow from a sword would kill another

705
00:52:28,775 --> 00:52:31,214
and blow from the spear with kill a third

706
00:52:31,440 --> 00:52:32,531
That's how they died.

707
00:52:33,613 --> 00:52:36,645
And these are the ones whom Allah revealed this Ayah(آية) about.

708
00:52:37,668 --> 00:52:40,991
So, their Islam did not benefit them,

709
00:52:42,342 --> 00:52:48,386
because they didn't make Hijrah(هجرة) and they went out with the army of Quraish(قُرَيْشْ).

710
00:52:48,648 --> 00:52:56,222
And I think, need to think very deeply about this particular situation because of the implications of it,

711
00:52:57,027 --> 00:52:58,966
the implications of it are very important.

712
00:52:59,580 --> 00:53:05,796
You don't want to die and then have the angels telling you that your reward is hellfire.

713
00:53:06,329 --> 00:53:09,476
We ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to forgive us all, to grant us Jannah(جنة).

714
00:53:09,912 --> 00:53:12,549
And we ask Him to spare us, from the punishment of hellfire.

715
00:53:13,573 --> 00:53:14,923
Another lesson; Istighasah(إستغاثه)

716
00:53:16,185 --> 00:53:17,880
seeking assistance from Allah.

717
00:53:19,029 --> 00:53:25,969
Rasool Allah ﷺ, after he prepared the army, and train them

718
00:53:26,912 --> 00:53:28,604
and lined them up

719
00:53:29,243 --> 00:53:33,468
and gave them his instructions and chose the best location.

720
00:53:34,890 --> 00:53:39,269
After all of that, he went aside and he started making Dua(دعا).

721
00:53:39,726 --> 00:53:41,449
And that is the meaning of Tawakkul(توكل).

722
00:53:42,810 --> 00:53:46,218
Tawakkul(توكل) means that you do your best.

723
00:53:47,659 --> 00:53:53,419
You exhaust the worldly means, and then you depend on Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

724
00:53:54,160 --> 00:54:04,905
So, Rasool Allah ﷺ, he did his best, in terms of everything that he was capable of doing, in this world

725
00:54:05,468 --> 00:54:08,533
 in terms of preparing for this battle.

726
00:54:09,081 --> 00:54:12,961
And after that, he started making Dua(دُعَا) to Allahعَزّوجَلّ.

727
00:54:14,239 --> 00:54:16,747
So, don't think that Allah will give you victory.

728
00:54:17,299 --> 00:54:21,823
If you sit at home comfortable on your couch

729
00:54:22,212 --> 00:54:24,858
 and just raise your hands and say O Allah, give me victory,

730
00:54:24,883 --> 00:54:28,323
O Allah give them victory, O Allah give the Muslim Ummah(امة) victory.

731
00:54:29,187 --> 00:54:30,989
You have to stand up and do something,

732
00:54:31,266 --> 00:54:35,089
you have to do your best and then you ask Allahعَزّوجَلّ to give you, and this applies to everything,

733
00:54:35,129 --> 00:54:36,414
This is the issue of Tawakkul(توكل).

734
00:54:36,723 --> 00:54:40,941
You know, some people have an understanding of Tawakkul(توكل)

735
00:54:40,991 --> 00:54:43,711
 that is not really Tawakkul(توكل), this is what is called Tawaakul(تواكل),

736
00:54:44,207 --> 00:54:49,110
like those whom were walking lazily, you know, pretending as if they are Zuhaad(زهاد).

737
00:54:49,676 --> 00:54:51,660
And Umar Ibn Al-Khattab(عمر ابن الخطاب) saw them, he said: Who are these?

738
00:54:51,700 --> 00:54:53,588
They said these are Al-Muttawakkiloon(ألمتوكلون).

739
00:54:53,707 --> 00:54:55,406
These are the ones, who have Tawakkal(توكل) in Allah.

740
00:54:55,963 --> 00:54:58,178
So, he went and beat them with his stick and said;

741
00:54:58,257 --> 00:55:01,970
you know that the sky doesn't rain, gold and silver, you have to go out and work.

742
00:55:03,256 --> 00:55:05,039
So the meaning of Tawakkul(توكل) is

743
00:55:05,206 --> 00:55:06,991
what Rasool Allah ﷺ mentioned in the Hadith(حديث),

744
00:55:07,047 --> 00:55:09,647
he said if you have the right Tawakkul(توكل) on Allah,

745
00:55:09,893 --> 00:55:13,845
Allah will give you, provide for you, like he provides for the birds,

746
00:55:14,246 --> 00:55:19,049
they leave in the morning hungry and they come back at evening full.

747
00:55:20,648 --> 00:55:25,573
So, here the birds didn't stay at home, they went out, worked for the entire day.

748
00:55:26,597 --> 00:55:28,098
And that is the meaning of Tawakkul(توكل).

749
00:55:29,440 --> 00:55:33,434
So, Tawakkul(توكل) is, you do your best but you do not depend on your effort,

750
00:55:34,120 --> 00:55:40,726
you do not depend on your intelligence, you do not dependent on anything in this world.

751
00:55:41,464 --> 00:55:42,766
 But you depend on Allah.

752
00:55:43,240 --> 00:55:45,786
So Yes, Rasool Allah ﷺ prepared the army,

753
00:55:45,826 --> 00:55:46,736
Yes, he lined them up,

754
00:55:46,776 --> 00:55:48,047
Yes, he gave them instructions

755
00:55:48,087 --> 00:55:49,326
but he didn't depend on that.

756
00:55:49,650 --> 00:55:53,772
He went aside And he started making Dua(دُعَا) and he was so involved in the Dua(دُعَا)

757
00:55:53,796 --> 00:55:57,918
and the Dua(دُعَا) was so long, Abu Bakr As-Siddique رضي الله عنه felt sorry for him,

758
00:55:58,446 --> 00:55:59,919
and said: O Rasool Allah, that's enough.

759
00:56:00,395 --> 00:56:03,683
 Allah will give you, what He promised to you, Allah already promised you.

760
00:56:05,025 --> 00:56:09,611
So, we have to have Istighasah(إستغاثه) on Allahعَزّوجَلّ, depend on Allahعَزّوجَلّ

761
00:56:10,024 --> 00:56:11,170
 but you also have to do your best.

762
00:56:12,155 --> 00:56:17,010
So, we don't just do our best and then forget about the Dua(دُعَا).

763
00:56:17,358 --> 00:56:21,237
And we don't just do the Dua(دُعَا) and forget about doing our best,

764
00:56:22,042 --> 00:56:24,078
they both go hand in hand.

765
00:56:25,757 --> 00:56:31,505
This is the end of our commentary on the Battle of Badr(بدر).

766
00:56:32,053 --> 00:56:33,670
In Sha Allah Ta'ala(اِن شاءالله تعالى) in our next session,

767
00:56:34,133 --> 00:56:38,321
we'll talk about events that occurred between Badr(بدر) and Uhud(أحَد).

768
00:56:39,108 --> 00:56:42,670
صَلَّى الله عَلى سَيَّدِنَا محمد وَعَلى اَلِهِ وَ صَحْبِهِ وَسَلمْ

769
00:56:43,045 --> 00:56:45,672
وَالسلام عليكم ورحمة الله وبركاته

